The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```
rcu_read_unlock();
```
Reason: The RCU read lock was released before accessing `opinfo->is_lease` and `opinfo->o_lease->version`, allowing a concurrent writer to free the memory and cause a use-after-free.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```
if (!opinfo || !opinfo->is_lease || opinfo->o_lease->version != 2) {
    rcu_read_unlock();
    return;
}
rcu_read_unlock();
```
Reason: The `rcu_read_unlock()` is called only after all RCU‑protected accesses (to `opinfo->is_lease` and `opinfo->o_lease->version`) have completed, preventing the use‑after‑free. The early return case also properly releases the lock before returning.

